==Latin==

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|rēgia|ann=1}}
* {{la-IPA|rēgiā|ann=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Substantive noun from an [[ellipsis]] of the [[collocative]] term ''domus regia'' ("royal home/dwelling/abode"), itself from {{m|la|domus|t=house, home, abode, dwelling}} and {{m|la|rēgius|t=of or pertaining to a king; regal, royal}}. Compare origin of Greek {{l|grc|βασιλική||t=basilica}}, from {{cog|gkm|-}} term {{m|grc|[[βασιλική]] [[στοά]]|t=royal building}}.

====Noun====
{{la-noun|rēgia<1>}}

# A [[royal]] [[palace]], [[castle]], [[fortress]], [[residence]]; [[court]]; [[kingship]].
# The royal [[tent]] in a [[camp]].
# A royal [[city]], [[capital]].
# A [[roofed]] [[colonnade]], [[portico]], [[hall]].

